		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4411&amp;p=33031#p33031"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Some more info about the 878<br><br>Capture.JPG</div></blockquote>We changed to using Celestrak for the data as it seemed to be consistently more accurate than Norad<br><br>The other link <a href="https://db.satnogs.org/api/transmitters/" class="postlink">https://db.satnogs.org/api/transmitters/</a>  does not contain keps. It seems to be a list of satellite transponder frequencies. However the satellite ID's don't seem to correspond to the Catalog number used in the keps data.<br><br>e.g. ISS is 25544U<br><br>e.g.<br><br><a href="https://www.satview.org/?sat_id=25544U" class="postlink">https://www.satview.org/?sat_id=25544U</a><br><br>I had to search on the freq of one of the ISS's transponders (145800) to find this data in that site<br><div class="codebox"><p>CODE: </p><pre><code>{        "uuid": "eozSf5mKyzNxoascs8V4bV",        "description": "Mode V/U FM - Voice Repeater",        "alive": true,        "type": "Transceiver",        "uplink_low": 145990000,        "uplink_high": null,        "uplink_drift": null,        "downlink_low": 437800000,        "downlink_high": null,        "downlink_drift": null,        "mode": "FM",        "mode_id": 1,        "uplink_mode": "FM",        "invert": false,        "baud": null,        "sat_id": "XSKZ-5603-1870-9019-3066",        "norad_cat_id": 25544,        "norad_follow_id": null,        "status": "active",        "updated": "2020-09-03T13:14:41.552071Z",        "citation": "https://www.ariss.org/press-releases/september-2-2020",        "service": "Amateur",        "iaru_coordination": "N/A",        "iaru_coordination_url": "",        "itu_notification": {            "urls": []        },        "frequency_violation": false,        "unconfirmed": false    },</code></pre></div>It looks like <br><br>"sat_id": "XSKZ-5603-1870-9019-3066",<br><br>is a NORAD code, but I've never seen any of keps data including this as its far too long to include within the character limit for the TLE data<br><br>Strangely, searching on "XSKZ-5603-1870-9019-3066" only seems to return results from db.satnogs.org, and even including NORAD in the search string doesn't give any useful results<br><br>Overall, I'm sceptical that satnogs data would be of any use, and how accurate it is.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Wed Sep 18, 2024 11:12 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
